# =============================================================================
# Docker build context — keep it to what the image is actually built from.
#
# This file is load-bearing, not housekeeping: the build context is uploaded
# to the daemon before a single instruction runs, and `target/` alone is
# multiple GB on a dev box. Every entry here is a layer-cache key that would
# otherwise be invalidated by editing an unrelated file.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Build outputs (both are rebuilt inside the image) ----
# `target/` is the big one: without this line the context upload alone takes
# minutes and every `COPY . .` busts the compile layer.
target/
**/target/
src-tauri/target/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# ---- Rust intermediate ----
# `src-tauri/gen/` is tauri-build output, regenerated on demand and
# gitignored — shipping it would just be a stale second copy.
src-tauri/gen/

# ---- VCS / CI / agent state ----
.git/
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.github/
.worktrees/
.scratch/
scripts/.scratch/
.minimax/
.playwright-mcp/
coverage/

# ---- Secrets ----
# Never bake a populated .env into an image; `.env.example` is not needed by
# any build stage either (the compose file documents the variables inline).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---- Tooling configs only the host lint uses ----
# The image runs `tsc -b` and `vite build`, never ESLint or Prettier.
eslint.config.js
.prettierrc
.prettierignore
.editorconfig

# ---- Docs & scratch (not build inputs) ----
*.md
docs/

# ---- Editor / OS cruft ----
.vscode/
.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
*~

# ---- Local run artifacts ----
*.log
npm-debug.log*
**/*.bak
**/*.removed
**/*.tmp.ts
**/*.tmp.cjs
build-exit.txt
build-output.txt
